  "title": "Human-AI collaboration for co-managing epilepsy in real time: scalp EEG and SEEG from 13 epilepsy monitoring unit patients",
  "description": "This dataset contains continuous scalp EEG from 11 patients and stereo-EEG (SEEG) from 2 patients, recorded during video-EEG monitoring in an epilepsy monitoring unit. The recordings support a prototype human-AI system in which a smartphone conversational agent collects patient and clinician feedback to retrain seizure detection models. The BIDS release includes EDF recordings, event annotations (seizures, patient events, sleep, medications), and derived model predictions from the original Pennsieve deposit.",
  "methods_description": "Patients underwent continuous video-EEG monitoring in the Penn Level 4 epilepsy monitoring unit, with scalp EEG sampled at 256 Hz and SEEG at 1024 Hz. Seizure detection used bandpass filtering (0.5-100 Hz scalp, 0.5-250 Hz iEEG), 60 and 120 Hz notch filtering, and common average or bipolar re-referencing. Annotations from clinicians and from patients via the smartphone platform were converted to BIDS events files.",
